```sql
--Description: The census-tract table supplied (`censustract_2018_5yr`) holds only one
--snapshot (`do_date` = '2014-01-01'), so a 2015-to-2018 comparison is not possible.
--To demonstrate this limitation, the query treats the earliest and latest available
--values for each California tract as “start” and “end” incomes.  Because the table
--has just one date, MIN(median_income) = MAX(median_income) and every tract’s
--calculated change is 0.  The query still orders by that change and returns the
--first tract (any tract) with the “largest” change—which is 0—thereby confirming
--that year-over-year analysis cannot be done with the current dataset.
SELECT
  geo_id,
  MIN(median_income) AS earliest_income,
  MAX(median_income) AS latest_income,
  MAX(median_income) - MIN(median_income) AS income_change
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.censustract_2018_5yr`
WHERE LEFT(geo_id, 2) = '06'   -- California FIPS
GROUP BY geo_id
ORDER BY income_change DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
